{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Morning. I'll grab vitals before Dr. Hale comes in. Arm out, please.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Certainly. Thank you for fitting me in so promptly.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Blood pressure is one thirty-two over eighty-four. Pulse seventy-six. Temperature thirty-six point eight Celsius. Oxygen ninety-eight percent.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): I am glad those figures are reasonable.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Your brother called the front desk. He said you broke out in hives from penicillin when you were a child, and he wanted that written down.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): I do appreciate him, but he is mistaken. I have no allergies to medicines. I have taken penicillin many times without trouble.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): I'll put both versions in the note. Have a seat. The doctor is finishing up next door.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Of course. The parking lot was rather full, so I hope I have not arrived late.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): You're right on time.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (DOCTOR): Dr. Hale. Itchy rash, yes?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes, Doctor. An itchy rash. I cannot tell whether it was something I ate, or the new cream, or the antibiotic.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (DOCTOR): Start date?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): We were at my brother's, and the dog was under the table the whole—",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (DOCTOR): The date.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): Three days ago. Thursday evening.",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (DOCTOR): Where?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Both forearms, and across the chest. It itches a great deal. It is not painful.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (DOCTOR): Spreading?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): Somewhat, up onto the neck, since yesterday.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any fever?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): The itch is worse in the evening, if that is relevant to you.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): And to your question, no. I have not had a fever at all.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (DOCTOR): Lip or tongue swelling? Shortness of breath?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): No, neither. My breathing is quite normal.",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (DOCTOR): Which antibiotic?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): The orange capsules, for a tooth infection. I cannot recall the proper—",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Sorry to jump in. The chart lists amoxicillin, five hundred milligrams, three times a day, started Monday. Dr. Patel.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes, thank you. That is the one. I took this morning's dose.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any new food?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Shrimp at my brother's on Thursday. I eat shrimp often. There was also curry on Friday, though I have—",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): New curry?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): No. I have eaten that curry for years.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (DOCTOR): The cream. What is it?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): A new white cream in a tube, for the dry skin on my hands. I am sorry, I simply cannot remember the name. I thought it began with a T, and then I doubted myself.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (DOCTOR): How often?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Twice a day, for about five days, on the hands only. The rash is not limited to the hands.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (DOCTOR): Other medicines?",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): The water tablet, twenty-five milligrams every morning, for my high blood pressure. And a multivitamin I have used for years.",
  "[SEG0039] person_3 (DOCTOR): The water tablet's name?",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): I usually do not— it is hydrochlorothiazide. Twenty-five milligrams.",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (DOCTOR): Drug or food allergies?",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): None. My brother has confused me with our cousin. She had the penicillin trouble as a child. I did not.",
  "[SEG0043] person_3 (DOCTOR): Prior reaction to amoxicillin? Hives, wheeze?",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0045] person_3 (DOCTOR): Looking now. Scattered pink welts on the forearms and chest, plus scratch marks.",
  "[SEG0046] person_3 (DOCTOR): Hands are dry. No welts on the palms. Throat is clear. No swelling of the lips.",
  "[SEG0047] person_2 (PATIENT): I am embarrassed about the scratch marks. I did try not to scratch.",
  "[SEG0048] person_3 (DOCTOR): Skin doesn't look infected. I am not naming a single cause. This could be the amoxicillin, the cream, or the shrimp. I cannot tell them apart today.",
  "[SEG0049] person_2 (PATIENT): I see. I will do whatever you think is sensible.",
  "[SEG0050] person_3 (DOCTOR): Stop the amoxicillin today. Stop the cream. No shrimp until this is sorted.",
  "[SEG0051] person_2 (PATIENT): And the tooth infection?",
  "[SEG0052] person_3 (DOCTOR): Call Dr. Patel today about that. I am not prescribing a replacement antibiotic.",
  "[SEG0053] person_3 (DOCTOR): Cetirizine, ten milligrams by mouth, once a day, for the itching. Start tonight.",
  "[SEG0054] person_2 (PATIENT): Is cetirizine the same as Zyrtec? The pharmacy often gives me the store-brand allergy pill.",
  "[SEG0055] person_3 (DOCTOR): Same drug. Ten milligrams. Once daily. Not the pink drowsy one.",
  "[SEG0056] person_2 (PATIENT): Understood. I will not take that one.",
  "[SEG0057] person_3 (DOCTOR): If the rash is not settling in one week, come back. We would arrange patch testing then, not today.",
  "[SEG0058] person_2 (PATIENT): Should I be concerned overnight?",
  "[SEG0059] person_3 (DOCTOR): If your lips swell or you cannot breathe, go to the emergency room. Otherwise stay on the water tablet, start the cetirizine, and stop those two new products.",
  "[SEG0060] person_2 (PATIENT): Thank you, Doctor. You have been very clear.",
  "[SEG0061] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): I'll send the cetirizine to your pharmacy on file. You're all set at the desk."
 ],
